{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Hand-written manga onomatopoeia glossary for plan section 3.4. SfxClassifier decides from the recognized text whether a region is onomatopoeia, and this glossary is both one of its inputs (the exact/normalized/repeat steps only) and the source of the card the sheet shows. A matched region is still translated (section 2.6); the gloss sits on top.",
    "license": "Original content written for this project. Section 8.4 flagged sourcing as open because published SFX lists carry unclear licensing; nothing here is copied from one.",
    "kind": "giongo = real sounds, giseigo = voices, gitaigo = manner/state (silent), gijougo = feelings (silent)",
    "matching": "Lookup normalizes katakana to hiragana and strips long vowels, small tsu, tildes and spacing, then tries exact match, then the doubled/halved form, then longest prefix."
